ts of raw flour. these always turn out fluffy and golden. <br> <br>They’re crispy on the outside and buttery and soft on the inside.Operator error. I had some buttermilk that I used instead milk and used 2 bananas like some other reviewers.- so good.Definitely , a keeper- thank you!I made this this morning. Thanks for offering such great recipes. However, now I just make them on my electric griddle with non-stick spray. I’ve tried quite a lot of banana pancakes recipes but this one tops it. <br> <br>Yum!Great recipe! So easy to make and light in texture. We make double or triple batches (depending on the number of bananas we have lying around) and freeze them for quick breakfasts during the week. VERY easy to make too!I am compelled to write a review! They were easy enough to make with my boys and we loved to do it together and we loved the pancakes. I usually skip breakfast, but the smell of it convinced me to have one and I’m glad I did. Perfect.I’ve tried your banana pancake recipe, and it was delicious! So easy and for the first time I think EVER, I didn’t burn pancakes! I’m sure I’m not your only European based reader who looks at all those cup measurements and sighs.Hi Eliza, I actually do have metric measurements for most recipes on the site. The only change I have made is substituting half of the flour with whole WHITE wheat flour. <br> <br> Just a little extra touch This is the best banana pancake recipe by far (and I’ve tried a few!). Since our Honeymoon, almost 18 yrs ago,  we’ve (my hubby & I) been looking & trying recipes for Banana Pancakes, which we ate for breakfast at the buffet every am at Sandals St. Lucia for our 8 day stay. !What are the calories and nutrional content for this recipe? I threw in some frozen blueberries into the mix as well. Brings us back to our Honeymoon at Sandals @ La Toc in St. Lucia! My 3 year old loves them, we drizzle a bit of honey and sprinkle someWow! <br> <br>I made a lot of modifications, because that is just what I 